  "question": {
    "text": "In the given circuit, rms value of current (Irms) through the resistor $R$ is :<br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/aHaZk2pei9iFEQ9YHqBkmjmbU2nf5eV9CESgR6GnNIM.original.fullsize.png\"><br>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "S5lMf",
      "text": "$2 \\mathrm{~A}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "bIv4Y",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{2} \\mathrm{~A}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NmhFv",
      "text": "$20 \\mathrm{~A}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "5DOMR",
      "text": "$2 \\sqrt{2} \\mathrm{~A}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "(a) Given,<br />Capacitive reactance, $\\mathrm{X}_{\\mathrm{C}}=100 \\Omega$<br />Inductive reactance, $\\mathrm{X}_{\\mathrm{L}}=200 \\Omega$<br />Resistance, $R=100 \\Omega$<br />Impedance, $\\mathrm{Z}=\\sqrt{\\mathrm{R}^2+\\left(\\mathrm{X}_{\\mathrm{L}}-\\mathrm{X}_{\\mathrm{C}}\\right)^2}$<br />$Z=\\sqrt{100^2+(200-100)^2}=100 \\sqrt{2} \\Omega$<br />RMS value of current,<br />$i_{\\mathrm{rms}}=\\frac{V_{\\mathrm{rms}}}{Z}=\\frac{200 \\sqrt{2}}{100 \\sqrt{2}}=2 \\mathrm{~A}$",
    "image": null
  },
